	'k052b37db' => 'Awake at 3 a.m.',
	'k05bf54a9' => 'In-lab night study in our private room',
	'k05dbc2cf' => 'How a night is read',
	'k066bebc5' => 'Dr. Tomas Varga is a sleep physician specializing in sleep-related breathing disorders, complex sleep apnea, and nocturnal hypoventilation. Dr. Varga evaluates patient diagnostic recordings, reviews airflow and oxygenation data, and guides individuals toward appropriate airway therapies. He works in close coordination with ENT surgeons and dental specialists when patients require structural airway interventions or custom oral appliances to maintain open nocturnal respiration.',
	'k06b2d7a5' => 'The physician reading is part of every study price; the separate 45-minute results visit is $140.',
	'k06e114a1' => 'Struggling to stay awake during afternoon meetings, experiencing heavy mental fog, or needing multiple cups of coffee just to remain functional are signs of significant daytime sleepiness. This is not simply a personal failing or lack of willpower; it indicates that your sleep architecture is missing restorative deep sleep or is being continuously fragmented by micro-arousals. To investigate persistent hypersomnolence, we examine your sleep quality, duration, and nocturnal breathing. We often recommend a full overnight study in our study room to measure electroencephalographic sleep stages, heart rate changes, and limb movements. Understanding whether your fatigue stems from unrefreshing sleep stages, hidden breathing pauses, or another physiological cause is the first step toward effective relief.',
	'k07478946' => 'How a night study works',
