	'k0837cc63' => 'Mei, 34, ICU nurse',
	'k09f11c1d' => 'The page you were looking for is not here. Try the menu above, or go back to the start.',
	'k0b6544f8' => 'Sleep apnea and persistent snoring',
	'k0b8bd8e7' => 'Evening',
	'k0d5e9fb7' => 'Medical director, sleep physician',
	'k0e8e3767' => 'We check the night first, then the habits around it.',
	'k0ee0337d' => 'Nemuri Clinic is an evening sleep clinic in Seattle for working adults. We listen first, record one night at home or in our study room, and sit with you to read it.',
	'k0f329543' => 'Daniel, a 52-year-old bus dispatcher, never believed he had a sleep problem until his partner raised serious concerns. Daniel assumed his heavy afternoon drowsiness was simply the natural consequence of long working hours, but his partner noticed loud, irregular snoring punctuated by sudden silences where his breathing seemed to stop completely before gasping back to life. Daniel booked an evening consultation with Dr. Tomas Varga, who recommended a full overnight study in our private Seattle study room. Senior technologist Owen Mbeki monitored Daniel\'s sleep from 20:30 until 07:00, capturing unequivocal evidence of obstructive sleep apnea with frequent breathing pauses and corresponding oxygen desaturations throughout the night. At his results visit, Daniel reviewed his hypnogram and began CPAP therapy with nurse Grace Lin. Grace guided him through personalized mask fitting, pressure adjustments, and comfort coaching, followed by a four-week compliance data review. With steady airway support, Daniel eliminated his nocturnal breathing pauses and regained sustained daytime alertness.',
	'k135471a6' => 'Returning home as the sun rises makes restorative rest difficult to protect against daylight and city noise.',
	'k13c7d2d7' => 'Sat',
	'k14674ed6' => 'Before you book',
	'k14a29845' => 'Owen Mbeki serves as our senior sleep technologist, bringing extensive physiological monitoring expertise to our single private overnight study room. Owen oversees all in-lab polysomnography recordings from check-in at 20:30 until wake-up at 07:00. His calm, meticulous approach to sensor placement and continuous overnight monitoring ensures patient comfort, maintains data integrity throughout the night, and provides physicians with immaculate data for precise clinical interpretation.',
	'k1578d234' => 'Will my health insurance policy cover consultations and sleep studies?',
	'k15ca1ddb' => 'You do not need a physician referral to schedule an appointment at Nemuri Clinic. As an independent, self-pay medical practice, we welcome direct bookings from individuals seeking specialized sleep evaluations. However, if your primary care provider has already completed preliminary health screenings or documented specific medical concerns, we encourage you to bring those medical records or laboratory results to your first consultation. Having your previous clinical history allows our physicians to coordinate effectively with your overall healthcare team while assessing your sleep health.',
	'k1673e069' => 'Dr. Hana Ellery founded Nemuri Clinic specifically to serve working adults who find it difficult or impossible to take time off during standard daytime business hours. Taking half a day off from work to attend medical appointments frequently discourages patients from seeking necessary care. By scheduling consultations from 13:00 to 17:00 and 17:30 to 21:00 Tuesday through Friday, along with Saturday appointments from 09:00 to 15:00, we make specialized sleep medicine accessible without disrupting your professional schedule.',
	'k186a5e4f' => 'What happens if I have trouble falling asleep during the in-lab night study?',
	'k18bae8f4' => 'Nemuri Clinic operates as a self-pay medical practice in Seattle, providing transparent and straightforward pricing in USD for all consultations, diagnostic sleep studies, and treatment programmes. We provide an itemised receipt for every visit so you can submit claims to your insurance provider.',
	'k1ad47dbe' => 'Malik Hassan — Front Desk &amp; Scheduling',
	'k1bcae746' => 'One room, one person',
	'k1ef1eb09' => 'How we work',
	'k2036c877' => 'Enough hours in bed, yet the afternoon is a struggle to stay alert.',
	'k2044f844' => 'We look closely at nocturnal sleep architecture and daytime fatigue patterns to find why your rest is not restoring you.',
	'k20b1203c' => 'six weekly 50-min sessions with a sleep psychologist',
	'k21957bfd' => 'Read the story',
	'k22d805e0' => 'Or at home',
	'k23299dc3' => 'Our private study room offers a calm, domestic space with quiet linens, soft lighting, and minimal clinical distraction. A qualified sleep technologist monitors your overnight recording from the adjacent room from check-in at 20:30 until departure at 07:00, ensuring complete attentiveness throughout the night.',
	'k23b6e5b6' => 'A take-home sleep test showed no breathing interruptions. Through six weekly CBT-I sessions with our sleep psychologist and a consistent rise time, she rebuilt her confidence in staying asleep.',
	'k24f32d45' => 'Our overnight capacity is deliberately one person per night. The room is private and dim, and the technologist stays awake at the desk next door until you leave at 07:00.',
	'k267cf93e' => 'Can\'t stay asleep?',
	'k26b3e31c' => 'Plan a first visit',
	'k2791dfa7' => 'We review your shift schedule and light exposure to design a sleep timing routine that supports restorative daytime rest.',
	'k27e93a7d' => 'Dr. Tomas Varga — Sleep Physician',
	'k28b34e40' => 'The study room',
	'k29aeeab4' => 'Dr. Priya Raman leads our Cognitive Behavioural Therapy for Insomnia (CBT-I) programme, helping adults overcome persistent sleep-onset difficulties and early morning awakenings. Over six weekly 50-minute sessions, Dr. Raman guides patients through evidence-based behavioral realignment, stimulus control, and sleep restriction techniques. Her compassionate, structured methods empower individuals to rebuild sleep efficiency and achieve sustained, drug-free restoration of natural nocturnal sleep patterns.',
	'k2aaa9739' => 'Waking at 3 a.m. with a racing mind and an inability to drift back to sleep is one of the most common complaints we evaluate. You may feel physically exhausted yet mentally alert, watching the bedside clock while anxiety about tomorrow builds. During your initial consultation, we review your daily routines, stress factors, and bedroom environment, and we ask you to maintain our structured two-week sleep diary. If we need to rule out underlying nocturnal breathing disturbances, we may arrange a home sleep test. When insomnia is driven by conditioned arousal and irregular sleep schedules, structured psychological treatment such as CBT-I offers an evidence-based approach to rebuild sleep efficiency and establish a consistent morning rise time.',
	'k2b5e0a7e' => 'Why are clinic consultations offered exclusively in the afternoon and evening?',
	'k2da97c74' => 'Dr. Hana Ellery founded Nemuri Clinic in 2016 to offer Seattle working adults comprehensive sleep medicine during practical evening hours. As medical director, she oversees all diagnostic evaluations and clinical protocols. Dr. Ellery believes deeply in unhurried patient communication, taking time during 60-minute initial consultations and 45-minute results visits to review overnight sleep traces collaboratively and build personalized recovery plans that address both biological disruption and daytime demands.',
	'k2dd64c1e' => 'Owen Mbeki',
	'k2ddecde8' => 'Tue',
	'k2df7189e' => 'If you find it nearly impossible to fall asleep before 2 a.m. or 3 a.m. and struggle bitterly when an alarm forces you awake for typical morning business hours, you may have a delayed sleep phase. This condition occurs when your internal biological clock runs substantially later than the conventional social clock. You sleep soundly and wake refreshed when allowed to follow your natural schedule, but mandatory early mornings cause chronic sleep debt. We evaluate your circadian profile using detailed sleep diary tracking over fourteen consecutive days. We then design a gradual circadian resetting protocol, utilizing timed morning light exposure and consistent rise times to align your natural rhythm with your daily responsibilities.',
	'k2eb1e455' => 'Parking facilities and building entry',
	'k30a6f60f' => 'Stories are shared with permission and names changed. Every night is different. Because individual biology, health history, and daily routines vary considerably, our clinical team focuses on meticulous diagnostic measurements and personalized sleep management rather than generalized assumptions. We do not make claims of fixed outcomes or universal treatment response rates. We encourage every person experiencing persistent nocturnal waking, daytime exhaustion, or breathing pauses to undergo a thorough clinical evaluation to discover the precise factors affecting their rest.',
	'k317ca755' => 'Step 4: Results visit within 10 days',
	'k32964a49' => 'A partner notices pauses or loud snoring. You may wake unrefreshed and not know why.',
	'k337ba22b' => 'Your care begins when you reach out by telephone at (206) 555-0142 or schedule an appointment through our website. Malik Hassan at our front desk will assist you in selecting an afternoon or evening consultation time that fits around your work commitments. Before you arrive at Suite 210 on Alder Lane, we ask you to prepare a complete list of your current medications, your photo identification, and any personal notes you have kept regarding your sleep difficulties. We ensure all preliminary intake details are handled smoothly so your appointment starts promptly.',
	'k33986c34' => 'Sleeping after the night shift — Mei\'s story',
	'k35777e8a' => 'Plain answers about cost',
	'k36ac39c0' => 'We explain the findings in plain English and map out the next steps together.',
	'k3a4c53e8' => 'Specialist referrals and collaborative care',
	'k3a7f9f48' => 'For patients driving to afternoon or evening appointments, convenient street parking and nearby commercial parking garages are located within immediate walking distance of our building on Alder Lane. If you are arriving for an evening consultation after 18:00 or checking in for an overnight sleep study at 20:30, please note that the main exterior building doors lock automatically for nighttime security. Simply use the intercom buzzer located beside the street entrance to contact our staff, and our technologist will promptly buzz you inside.',
	'k3a9a1590' => 'When symptoms are complex, involving insomnia, unusual nighttime movements, or unrefreshing sleep of unclear origin, we conduct a full overnight polysomnography in our private clinic suite. You check in at 20:30, entering a quiet, dim bedroom designed with comfortable furnishings, pale linen, and acoustic privacy. A sleep technologist gently applies surface sensors to your scalp, face, chest, and legs using gentle medical adhesive. These sensors monitor brainwave activity, eye movements, muscle tone, heart rhythm, respiratory effort, and oxygen saturation without pain. You settle into sleep at your customary bedtime. In the morning, you wake naturally by 07:00, the sensors are gently removed, and you enjoy a warm cup of coffee before heading to work. The $1,250 fee includes your stay, continuous monitoring, and detailed physician analysis.',
	'k3ac54ee0' => 'You fall asleep without trouble, but wake in the middle of the night and cannot drift back off.',
	'k3cbe8173' => '30 min',
	'k3d57fe5a' => 'We believe patients should never have to endure long, anxious waits for diagnostic test results. Following your home sleep test or in-lab polysomnography study, your physiological data is analyzed carefully and reviewed by our sleep physician. Your comprehensive 45-minute results visit is scheduled within 10 days of your study completion. During this visit, your physician personally explains your hypnogram and respiratory readings in detail, answering all of your questions and collaboratively mapping out your treatment plan.',
	'k3d69a642' => 'Diagnostic sleep testing often leaves patients with opaque medical summaries, confusing numerical indices, and little practical understanding of their condition. At Nemuri Clinic, we believe the diagnostic process is complete only when you understand what your night looked like. At your 45-minute results visit, scheduled within 10 days of your study, Dr. Hana Ellery or Dr. Tomas Varga sits beside you to review your sleep graphs step by step. We look at your sleep stages, awakenings, airflow changes, and oxygen levels together, explaining every finding in clear, plain language. We never hand you a generic prescription or rush you toward a single predetermined therapy. Instead, we discuss how your physiological data connects with your daily fatigue and collaborate with you on a sensible, sustainable path forward.',
	'k3e4b55ec' => 'Evening 1',
	'k3e4c0855' => 'Patient privacy and clinical expectations',
	'k41009180' => 'Daniel, 52, a bus dispatcher. A night in our study room found breathing pauses. Grace Lin set up his CPAP and checked it with him at four weeks.',
	'k43340e6c' => 'Read more',
	'k436fef75' => 'How the night is read',
	'k43700e64' => 'Book a first consultation',
	'k43ee8d4b' => 'Misalignments between your internal circadian pacemaker and your required waking schedule can severely disrupt sleep onset and morning alertness. For patients dealing with delayed sleep phase syndrome or rotating shift rosters, we formulate customized circadian realignment plans. These protocols combine strategically timed bright light exposure, daylight management using blue-light filtering glasses or blackout curtains, and precise scheduling of evening winding-down periods. By gradually shifting your core body clock markers, we help synchronize your biological sleep drive with your social and occupational demands. This approach provides sustainable, non-pharmacological support for shift workers, healthcare professionals, and late chronotypes striving to maintain dependable rest on demanding Seattle schedules.',
	'k4686a42f' => 'Founded in 2016, Nemuri Clinic is an evening sleep-medicine clinic in Seattle designed for working adults who struggle to fall or stay asleep. We provide thorough diagnostic evaluations and evidence-based sleep care during hours that fit your working life.',
	'k471a7034' => 'Your first consultation is an unhurried, 60-minute meeting with a sleep physician, priced at $180. During this hour, we listen closely to your history, discussing when your sleep problems began, your daily energy levels, and your nighttime habits. We conduct a targeted physical and upper airway examination. At the conclusion of this visit, your physician provides you with our structured two-week sleep diary. Recording your daily bedtime, wake-up times, nocturnal awakenings, and daytime fatigue over fourteen consecutive days provides essential baseline data that informs our subsequent diagnostic and treatment decisions.',
	'k47231243' => 'No promises, only a clear plan',
