	'k5219db08' => 'Sleeping after night shifts',
	'k523eedb6' => 'Hours and access',
	'k541f8ba9' => 'Evening sleep medicine for working adults.<br>Suite 210, 88 Alder Lane, Seattle, WA 98101',
	'k54490a8d' => 'Circadian timing and light therapy',
	'k551baf56' => 'You fall asleep without trouble, then wake in the middle of the night and cannot drift back off.',
	'k555c7cae' => 'Back to the home page',
	'k55a1aca2' => 'Loud, chronic snoring is frequently observed first by a sleeping partner, who may also notice frightening pauses where breathing stops entirely followed by sudden gasps or snorts. People experiencing obstructive sleep apnea often wake with a dry mouth, morning headaches, and an unrefreshing sense of rest, regardless of how many hours they spent in bed. Sleep physician Dr. Tomas Varga evaluates these upper airway disruptions using either a portable one-night home sleep test or a comprehensive overnight study in our Seattle study room. These recordings monitor airflow, respiratory effort, and blood oxygen saturation to quantify breathing pauses accurately. Once diagnosed, interventions such as CPAP coaching with nurse Grace Lin can restore continuous nocturnal breathing.',
	'k57ca058b' => 'one-night recorder, set-up visit and physician reading',
	'k58782f03' => 'Heavy afternoons at work',
	'k5b5b2584' => 'An irresistible urge to move your legs when resting in the evening, often accompanied by unpleasant creeping, crawling, or tingling sensations deep inside your calves, is characteristic of restless legs syndrome. These sensations typically intensify when you lie down in bed, forcing you to stretch, pace the floor, or massage your muscles to achieve temporary relief, severely delaying sleep onset. During your consultation, we review your symptom timing, medication history, and relevant metabolic blood markers such as iron storage levels. We also assess whether periodic limb movements are occurring during sleep. Treatment focuses on addressing identifiable nutritional or pharmacological triggers and establishing evening settling routines to calm neuromuscular excitability before bedtime.',
	'k5b753584' => 'Heavy afternoons',
	'k5b9b468d' => 'One room, one night, one person awake for you.',
	'k5c6f657a' => 'We believe in complete financial transparency with no hidden laboratory charges or surprise facility fees. Our initial consultation lasts 60 minutes with a sleep physician, includes a comprehensive medical review, and provides you with a two-week sleep diary for $180. Follow-up consultations lasting 30 minutes are priced at $95. When diagnostic sleep recording is indicated, our portable home sleep test costs $320, which covers the one-night recorder, clinic set-up instruction, and physician interpretation. A full overnight study in our private Seattle room costs $1,250, including overnight stay, technologist monitoring from 20:30 to 07:00, and full polysomnographic analysis. Following any study, a 45-minute results visit to review your sleep graphs with your physician is $140.',
	'k5d220097' => 'Reading the night together',
	'k5d29295c' => 'Alder Lane, Seattle',
	'k5d909ae6' => 'Sleep medicine should fit into the rhythm of working life. We hold our consultations in the evening so you never have to take time off work to be seen, listening carefully to your history before recommending an objective diagnostic test.',
	'k5e706a9b' => 'Visit',
	'k5f9a2aa2' => 'Also at the clinic',
	'k6229c8f8' => 'Delayed sleep phase and late body clocks',
	'k6506c819' => 'Working rotating shifts, overnight rosters, or irregular schedules places severe strain on human biology. Healthcare workers, emergency personnel, transit staff, and hospitality employees often find themselves forced to sleep when daylight and internal circadian rhythms signal alertness. You may experience fragmented daytime sleep, stomach upset, and profound fatigue when your shift begins. We evaluate shift-work sleep problems by mapping your current roster against your biological circadian rhythm using your two-week sleep diary. Rather than prescribing blanket solutions, our team constructs individualized schedules that combine scheduled light exposure, light-blocking strategies, and tailored sleep windows. This structured planning helps anchor your rest periods around your working commitments without relying on unsustainable medication cycles.',
	'k652a82c8' => 'Sleeping after the night shift',
	'k660de002' => 'Our approach',
	'k6620adf7' => 'Your night study is never recorded unattended by automated software. Senior sleep technologist Owen Mbeki and sleep technologist Lucía Ferrer oversee all overnight polysomnography studies from our dedicated control station directly adjacent to the study room. They monitor real-time physiological signal traces across the night, checking sensor impedance and ensuring data integrity while you rest peacefully. If a sensor becomes loose while you shift in bed, our technologist can quietly reposition it with minimal disruption to your sleep. Having an experienced technologist on watch ensures the safety and precision of your study, producing pristine clinical data that gives your physician an accurate, reliable basis for interpretation.',
	'k66ecb41c' => 'Line by line, with you',
	'k673d11c6' => 'When to see your own doctor first',
	'k68d95c10' => 'What your sleep reading reveals',
	'k69242754' => 'Six weekly 50-minute sessions with Dr. Priya Raman, our sleep psychologist, built on a two-week sleep diary. $780.',
	'k6ab9375e' => 'Tel.',
	'k6ad1ad2c' => 'Dr. Hana Ellery — Medical Director &amp; Sleep Physician',
	'k713cda42' => 'one night of full polysomnography, technologist on watch, reading',
	'k71cb85ae' => 'Effective sleep medicine does not rely on quick fixes or temporary sedatives. Following your diagnostic results visit, we develop personalized treatment plans focused on proven behavioral programmes, respiratory support, and circadian realignment.',
	'k731f8a14' => 'We begin with a 60-minute evening consultation with a sleep physician. We listen to your history, review your daytime challenges, and hand you a two-week sleep diary to track your patterns.',
	'k772da7cf' => 'Itemised receipt provided for every visit. Self-pay fees in USD. We cannot promise what your insurer will reimburse. Cancellation with less than 24 h notice: $60.',
	'k77355267' => 'The entrance is on Alder Lane, with a lamp lit from late afternoon.',
	'k77604b7f' => 'We build a light and sleep-timing plan around your actual schedule.',
	'k79238d4d' => 'Runs the overnight studies, from check-in at 20:30 to departure at 07:00.',
	'k79327893' => 'Quiet, unhurried, precise',
	'k7a604108' => 'After completing your one-night home sleep test, you simply place the recorder, chest belt, finger clip, and nasal sensor back into the protective carry pouch provided. You return the kit directly to our front desk at Suite 210, 88 Alder Lane the following morning during regular clinic operating hours. Sleep technologist Lucía Ferrer checks the equipment in, downloads your physiological recording data immediately, and prepares the study for physician analysis ahead of your scheduled results visit.',
	'k7a967aa0' => 'Dr. Priya Raman — Sleep Psychologist',
	'k7af67582' => 'Clinic opening hours and consultation schedule',
	'k7c16f89a' => 'About the clinic',
	'k7c5f1f1d' => 'Ana, 41, a project manager. Her home test showed no breathing problem. She did six CBT-I sessions and settled on a fixed rise time.',
	'k7ca408a8' => 'We recognize that unpredictable work deadlines and family emergencies occur. If you need to cancel or reschedule an upcoming consultation, home test setup, or overnight night study, we require at least 24 hours of advance notice by telephone or email. This courtesy enables us to offer the reserved appointment time to another patient awaiting evaluation. Cancellations or missed appointments made with less than 24 hours of notice incur a fixed cancellation fee of $60.',
	'k7cd7017a' => 'Depending on your specific symptoms, we arrange an objective recording of your sleep using either a portable home test or an overnight study in our Seattle clinic. For home testing, Lucía Ferrer provides your recorder kit and set-up guidance during an afternoon visit. For complex sleep difficulties, you stay overnight in our private room, checking in at 20:30. Senior technologist Owen Mbeki attaches painless scalp and body sensors to record sleep stages, breathing patterns, and heart rate while you sleep comfortably, concluding at 07:00 with fresh morning coffee.',
	'k7daf97de' => 'The entrance',
	'k7e29cd13' => 'Results visits happen within 10 days of the recorded night. Forty-five minutes, the physician and you, the recording on the table.',
	'k7f32bf2f' => 'Most commercial sleep centres operate multiple beds in anonymous laboratory environments that feel clinical and hurried. We deliberately chose a different path. Nemuri Clinic maintains just one private overnight study room, furnished with a comfortable bed, pale linen, soft lighting, and quiet acoustic insulation. When you stay with us for an in-lab polysomnography study, you are the only patient in the clinic. Senior sleep technologist Owen Mbeki monitors your physiological signals throughout the night from his adjoining control desk, maintaining vigilant, unhurried attention on your sleep architecture, respiratory patterns, and oxygenation. There are no competing bells, no unfamiliar ward sounds, and no rushed morning discharges. You check in calmly at 20:30, wake naturally by 07:00, and leave with a warm cup of coffee ready for your morning.',
	'k7f793462' => 'Mei, 34, an ICU nurse on rotating shifts. We built a light and sleep-timing plan around her roster.',
	'k81f6cf10' => 'Location and public transit access',
	'k82b29968' => 'Your sleep diary if you have one, a list of medicines, and any earlier sleep results.',
	'k83f6c2c6' => 'The overnight recording generates a comprehensive sleep architecture chart called a hypnogram. Rather than offering a single score, the hypnogram maps your journey through the different physiological stages of sleep across the night, showing how smoothly you transition from light sleep into deep slow-wave restoration and rapid-eye-movement dream states. It documents exactly when micro-arousals occur, whether your oxygen saturation dips, and how muscle tension or breathing pauses disrupt sleep continuity. It is important to note that sleep medicine cannot promise a definitive diagnosis from a single night of recording, as sleep varies naturally; however, this objective trace provides an invaluable roadmap for your physician during your results visit.',
	'k842a77ad' => 'For fourteen consecutive days, you record your bedtimes, waking episodes, and daily routines.',
	'k85030722' => 'What people arrive with',
	'k8657e28b' => 'We examine your sleep patterns and nighttime habits, checking whether underlying breathing issues or conditioned arousal keep you awake.',
	'k88a79ce5' => 'Reading included in studies',
	'k8973ce0f' => 'Step 5: Personalized plan and follow-up care',
	'k8c7568f3' => 'CPAP set-up and first-month check',
	'k8db7ec95' => 'Five more people, seven in all',
	'k8dece703' => 'Grace Lin is a dedicated nurse and clinical CPAP coach who guides patients through equipment setup and therapy acclimatization. During initial equipment fittings and four-week follow-up checks, Grace addresses mask comfort, humidity levels, and pressure settings. Her practical coaching and continuous support help individuals adapt smoothly to continuous airway therapy, achieving consistent nightly comfort, clear breathing, and reliable daytime energy.',
	'k9029ccab' => 'You may believe you slept through the night, yet someone close to you noticed loud snoring or pauses in your breath.',
	'k91d3333b' => 'Continuous Positive Airway Pressure (CPAP) support',
	'k9266f2e5' => 'Step 3: Recording your night',
	'k94420571' => 'We record a single night of sleep, either in your own bed with a compact take-home recorder or in our private clinic room with full polysomnography monitored by a sleep technologist.',
	'k94b9dc19' => 'An overnight study in our clinic room revealed repeated breathing pauses. Following CPAP set-up and a four-week coaching check with Grace, his nocturnal breathing stabilized.',
	'k95223cb9' => 'The snoring someone else heard',
	'k95ffa0a1' => 'Suite 210, 88 Alder Lane<br>Seattle, WA 98101',
